   "note": "The painted REVENGE and TARGETS plates, and the glow over REVENGE, are erased row by row from the dark band of scene left of them (x 164-180), from the subtitle's last row to the gold rule they stand on (y 255-352), the first 11 rows fading from the painting into the fill so the army behind falls into shadow instead of being cut off (fade_top): RAID's four short plates cover the band only from y 297 down, and what they leave showing has to read as the header's own dark rather than a box. It runs from the painting's gold rail (x 183) to the screen's edge rather than stopping where the old plates did: ending at x 921 cut a knight in half down a straight line: the tabs are tabs_sheet.json's plates now, drawn by TabStrip, and where they part the old ones showed through. On the rule itself, the old REVENGE plate's two gold feet and the diamond under its centre -- the painting's mark for the lit tab, which would have stayed under REVENGE whichever was lit -- are refilled from the plain rule beside them."
